\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces A comparison of the three correlation functions $E(\theta )$ versus the relative measurement angle $\theta $. The quantum (solid red) and classical (dashed green) correlations only achieve perfect anti-correlation ($E=-1$) at $\theta =0$. The hypothetical stronger-than-quantum correlation (dotted blue) is perfect for any angle $\theta \neq  \pi /2$.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:correlations}{{1}{2}{A comparison of the three correlation functions $E(\theta )$ versus the relative measurement angle $\theta $. The quantum (solid red) and classical (dashed green) correlations only achieve perfect anti-correlation ($E=-1$) at $\theta =0$. The hypothetical stronger-than-quantum correlation (dotted blue) is perfect for any angle $\theta \neq \pi /2$}{figure.1}{}}
